# Local AI-assistant brain — kept private/local, not shipped.
# NO TRAILING SLASH, deliberately. `.private/` matches a DIRECTORY only, and a session working in a
# git worktree reaches the real one through a SYMLINK -- which is a file, matches nothing here, and
# is staged by `git add -A`. That is F16 on this branch: the symlink reached the index of a PUBLIC
# repository, and removing it did not disarm the rule that let it in. Without the slash one rule
# covers the directory, a symlink to it, and a stray file of the same name.
CLAUDE.md
.claude
.private

# Stray logs
*.log

